IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-payments`
IMPORT `uc3-sch2-liability`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 2 (claimant treated as liable or not liable to make payments): tests of layer 1.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text).
--
-- EVERY EXPECTED VALUE IS WRITTEN HERE FROM THE TEXT, beside the assertion, before the file was run: none was copied from what the encoding printed.
-- Where an expected value rests on a reading the text does not settle, the comment names the fork in NOTES.md (U3-F15 which Part prevails, U3-F18 the combined holding).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers.

GIVEN relation IS A `Listed relation`
GIVETH A `Possible close relative`
`uc3 test — a relative` relation MEANS
    `Possible close relative` WITH
        `relation to the person` IS relation
        `relation of the partner to the person` IS `not a listed relation`

-- Part 1 paragraph 1.
-- Expected: a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or either member of a couple) is responsible gives TRUE; the other member of the couple gives TRUE only for a claimant who
-- is a member of a couple claiming as a single person and not by virtue of regulation 3(4); joint claimants with the other member liable give FALSE; neither gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1 — the claimant is treated as liable because of the person who is liable` (`Person who is liable to make the payments` WITH `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible` IS TRUE, `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member` IS FALSE) `a single claimant` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1 — the claimant is treated as liable because of the person who is liable` (`Person who is liable to make the payments` WITH `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible` IS FALSE, `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member` IS TRUE) `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1 — the claimant is treated as liable because of the person who is liable` (`Person who is liable to make the payments` WITH `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible` IS FALSE, `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member` IS TRUE) `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1 — the claimant is treated as liable because of the person who is liable` (`Person who is liable to make the payments` WITH `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible` IS FALSE, `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member` IS TRUE) `joint claimants` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1 — the claimant is treated as liable because of the person who is liable` (`Person who is liable to make the payments` WITH `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible` IS FALSE, `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member` IS FALSE) `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Part 1 paragraph 2: all four conditions. Expected: all four gives TRUE; each missing in turn gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2 — the claimant is treated as liable because the person who is liable has failed to pay` (`Failure to pay by the person who is liable` WITH `the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so` IS TRUE, `the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation` IS TRUE, `the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements` IS TRUE, `it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2 — the claimant is treated as liable because the person who is liable has failed to pay` (`Failure to pay by the person who is liable` WITH `the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so` IS FALSE, `the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation` IS TRUE, `the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements` IS TRUE, `it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2 — the claimant is treated as liable because the person who is liable has failed to pay` (`Failure to pay by the person who is liable` WITH `the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so` IS TRUE, `the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation` IS FALSE, `the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements` IS TRUE, `it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2 — the claimant is treated as liable because the person who is liable has failed to pay` (`Failure to pay by the person who is liable` WITH `the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so` IS TRUE, `the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation` IS TRUE, `the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements` IS FALSE, `it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2 — the claimant is treated as liable because the person who is liable has failed to pay` (`Failure to pay by the person who is liable` WITH `the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so` IS TRUE, `the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation` IS TRUE, `the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements` IS TRUE, `it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- Part 1 paragraph 3: the liability is waived by the person to whom it is owed, by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works, which that person would otherwise have carried out.
-- Expected: all three gives TRUE; each missing gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 3 — the claimant is treated as liable although the liability is waived for repair work` (`Waiver of liability for repair work` WITH `the liability to make payments is waived by the person to whom the liability is owed` IS TRUE, `the waiver is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation` IS TRUE, `the works are works which the person to whom the liability is owed would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 3 — the claimant is treated as liable although the liability is waived for repair work` (`Waiver of liability for repair work` WITH `the liability to make payments is waived by the person to whom the liability is owed` IS FALSE, `the waiver is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation` IS TRUE, `the works are works which the person to whom the liability is owed would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 3 — the claimant is treated as liable although the liability is waived for repair work` (`Waiver of liability for repair work` WITH `the liability to make payments is waived by the person to whom the liability is owed` IS TRUE, `the waiver is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation` IS FALSE, `the works are works which the person to whom the liability is owed would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 3 — the claimant is treated as liable although the liability is waived for repair work` (`Waiver of liability for repair work` WITH `the liability to make payments is waived by the person to whom the liability is owed` IS TRUE, `the waiver is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation` IS TRUE, `the works are works which the person to whom the liability is owed would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- Part 1 paragraph 4: where the arrangements provide for rent free periods, the claimant is treated as liable for rent payments and service charge payments for the whole of any rent free period.
-- Expected: rent payments and service charge payments in a rent free period give TRUE; owner-occupier payments give FALSE (the paragraph names only the two kinds);
-- arrangements that provide for no rent free period give FALSE; a period in which the renter is still liable for every payment gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4 — the claimant is treated as liable for the whole of a rent free period` `rent payments` TRUE (`Period of the arrangements` WITH `the renter has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4 — the claimant is treated as liable for the whole of a rent free period` `service charge payments` TRUE (`Period of the arrangements` WITH `the renter has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4 — the claimant is treated as liable for the whole of a rent free period` `owner-occupier payments` TRUE (`Period of the arrangements` WITH `the renter has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4 — the claimant is treated as liable for the whole of a rent free period` `rent payments` FALSE (`Period of the arrangements` WITH `the renter has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4 — the claimant is treated as liable for the whole of a rent free period` `rent payments` TRUE (`Period of the arrangements` WITH `the renter has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 2 paragraph 5: liability owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and is (a) the other member of the couple, (b) a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant
-- (or the other member) is responsible, or (c) a close relative of the claimant, the other member, or a child within (b).
-- which: 0 none of those; 1 the other member; 2 a child; 3 a close relative of the claimant (a brother); 4 a close relative of the other member (a parent-in-law); 5 a close relative of a child within (b) (a sister).
GIVEN lives IS A BOOLEAN
      which IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Person to whom a liability is owed`
`uc3 test — a creditor` lives which MEANS
    `Person to whom a liability is owed` WITH
        `the person lives in the accommodation` IS lives
        `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member` IS which EQUALS 1
        `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member) is responsible` IS which EQUALS 2
        `the person as a possible close relative of the claimant` IS `uc3 test — a relative` (IF which EQUALS 3 THEN `a brother` ELSE `not a listed relation`)
        `the person as a possible close relative of the other member of the couple` IS `uc3 test — a relative` (IF which EQUALS 4 THEN `a parent-in-law` ELSE `not a listed relation`)
        `the person as a possible close relative of a child or qualifying young person who falls within paragraph (b)` IS `uc3 test — a relative` (IF which EQUALS 5 THEN `a sister` ELSE `not a listed relation`)

-- Expected: each of the five kinds who lives in the accommodation gives TRUE; any of them who does not live there gives FALSE; a person who lives there and is none of them gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5(1) — the liability is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and is within paragraph 5(1)(a) to (c)` (`uc3 test — a creditor` TRUE 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5(1) — the liability is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and is within paragraph 5(1)(a) to (c)` (`uc3 test — a creditor` TRUE 2) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5(1) — the liability is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and is within paragraph 5(1)(a) to (c)` (`uc3 test — a creditor` TRUE 3) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5(1) — the liability is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and is within paragraph 5(1)(a) to (c)` (`uc3 test — a creditor` TRUE 4) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5(1) — the liability is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and is within paragraph 5(1)(a) to (c)` (`uc3 test — a creditor` TRUE 5) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5(1) — the liability is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and is within paragraph 5(1)(a) to (c)` (`uc3 test — a creditor` FALSE 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5(1) — the liability is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and is within paragraph 5(1)(a) to (c)` (`uc3 test — a creditor` FALSE 3) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5(1) — the liability is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and is within paragraph 5(1)(a) to (c)` (`uc3 test — a creditor` TRUE 0) EQUALS FALSE

-- Paragraph 6(6), "associate" of A: the spouse or civil partner; a child or step-child if under 18; a trustee of a settlement in which A has a life interest; an undertaking of which A is a director;
-- an employee or partner; a person with whom A has an agreement about shares; a person with whom A has an agreement to act together on voting power.
-- which: 0 none; 1 spouse; 2 child; 3 trustee; 4 undertaking; 5 employee or partner; 6 share agreement; 7 voting agreement.
GIVEN which IS A NUMBER
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Person who may be an associate`
`uc3 test — a person who may be an associate` which age MEANS
    `Person who may be an associate` WITH
        `spouse or civil partner of A` IS which EQUALS 1
        `child or step-child of A` IS which EQUALS 2
        `age in complete years` IS age
        `trustee of a settlement under which A has a life interest in possession (in Scotland a life interest)` IS which EQUALS 3
        `undertaking of which A is a director` IS which EQUALS 4
        `employee or partner of A` IS which EQUALS 5
        `has with A an agreement or arrangement with respect to the acquisition, holding or disposal of shares or other interests in X or Y` IS which EQUALS 6
        `has with A an agreement or arrangement under which they undertake to act together in exercising their voting power in relation to X or Y` IS which EQUALS 7
-- Expected: each of the seven kinds gives TRUE (the child being 17); a child aged 18 gives FALSE (limb (b) says "if under 18"); none gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(6) — associate` (`uc3 test — a person who may be an associate` 1 40) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(6) — associate` (`uc3 test — a person who may be an associate` 2 17) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(6) — associate` (`uc3 test — a person who may be an associate` 2 18) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(6) — associate` (`uc3 test — a person who may be an associate` 3 40) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(6) — associate` (`uc3 test — a person who may be an associate` 4 40) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(6) — associate` (`uc3 test — a person who may be an associate` 5 40) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(6) — associate` (`uc3 test — a person who may be an associate` 6 40) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(6) — associate` (`uc3 test — a person who may be an associate` 7 40) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(6) — associate` (`uc3 test — a person who may be an associate` 0 40) EQUALS FALSE

-- A holder of an interest in C. isA: the holder is the person (A); assoc: the kind of associate (0 not an associate); limb: which of the measures the percentage belongs to:
-- 1 shares in C, 2 shares in the parent undertaking P, 3 voting rights in C, 4 voting rights in P; pct: the percentage; influence: 0 none, 1 significant influence by shareholding in C,
-- 2 by shareholding in P, 3 by voting rights in C, 4 by voting rights in P.
GIVEN isA IS A BOOLEAN
      assoc IS A NUMBER
      limb IS A NUMBER
      pct IS A NUMBER
      influence IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Holder of an interest in a company`
`uc3 test — a holder` isA assoc limb pct influence MEANS
    `Holder of an interest in a company` WITH
        `the holder is the person (A)` IS isA
        `the holder as a possible associate of the person` IS `uc3 test — a person who may be an associate` assoc 40
        `percentage of the shares in C held` IS IF limb EQUALS 1 THEN pct ELSE 0
        `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of the holder's shareholding in C` IS influence EQUALS 1
        `percentage of the shares in a parent undertaking (P) of C held` IS IF limb EQUALS 2 THEN pct ELSE 0
        `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of the holder's shareholding in P` IS influence EQUALS 2
        `percentage of the voting rights in C that the holder is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of` IS IF limb EQUALS 3 THEN pct ELSE 0
        `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of the holder's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in C` IS influence EQUALS 3
        `percentage of the voting rights in P that the holder is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of` IS IF limb EQUALS 4 THEN pct ELSE 0
        `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of the holder's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in P` IS influence EQUALS 4

-- Paragraph 6(4): A has a material interest in C if A (a) holds at least 10% of the shares in C, (b) can exercise significant influence over C by virtue of A's shareholding, (c) holds at least 10% of the shares in a
-- parent undertaking P of C, (d) significant influence over P by shareholding, (e) is entitled to exercise or control at least 10% of the voting rights in C, (f) significant influence over C by voting rights,
-- (g) at least 10% of the voting rights in P, (h) significant influence over P by voting rights.
-- Expected: 10% of any of the four measures gives TRUE; 9% of any gives FALSE; significant influence by any of the four ways gives TRUE even at 0%; no holding gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 10 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 9 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 2 10 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 2 9 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 3 10 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 3 9 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 4 10 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 4 9 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 0 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 0 2) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 0 3) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 0 4) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 0 0) EQUALS FALSE
-- Paragraph 6(5): "A" is the person, any associate, or the person and associates taken together (fork U3-F18: the combined holding is the one computed).
-- Expected: the person with 6% and the person's spouse with 5% of the shares in C: 11% together, TRUE; the person with 6% and a stranger (not an associate) with 5%: FALSE;
-- the person with 6% and the spouse with 3%: 9%, FALSE; an associate alone with 10% TRUE; a stranger alone with 10% FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 6 0, `uc3 test — a holder` FALSE 1 1 5 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 6 0, `uc3 test — a holder` FALSE 0 1 5 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 6 0, `uc3 test — a holder` FALSE 1 1 3 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` FALSE 5 1 10 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` FALSE 0 1 10 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(5)(c) — the percentage of the shares in C held by the person and the associates together` (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 6 0, `uc3 test — a holder` FALSE 1 1 5 0, `uc3 test — a holder` FALSE 0 1 20 0) EQUALS 11

-- Paragraph 6(1): the owners or directors of the company include the claimant, the other member, a qualifying young person for whom either is responsible, or a close relative of any of them
-- who lives in the accommodation with the claimant. An "owner" is a person with a material interest (6(3)); a director is an owner or director.
-- A person who may be an owner or director: director, and a list of holdings.
GIVEN director IS A BOOLEAN
      holdings IS A LIST OF `Holder of an interest in a company`
GIVETH A `Person who may be an owner or director of a company`
`uc3 test — a person who may run the company` director holdings MEANS
    `Person who may be an owner or director of a company` WITH
        `is a director of the company` IS director
        `the holdings of the person and the person's associates` IS holdings

GIVETH A `Person who may be an owner or director of a company`
`uc3 test — a person who has nothing to do with the company` MEANS
    `uc3 test — a person who may run the company` FALSE EMPTY

-- Expected for 6(1): the person is an owner or director if a director (TRUE), or if holding 10% (TRUE), but not holding 9% (FALSE), and not neither (FALSE).
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the person is an owner or director of the company` (`uc3 test — a person who may run the company` TRUE EMPTY) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the person is an owner or director of the company` (`uc3 test — a person who may run the company` FALSE (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 10 0)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the person is an owner or director of the company` (`uc3 test — a person who may run the company` FALSE (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 9 0)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the person is an owner or director of the company` `uc3 test — a person who has nothing to do with the company` EQUALS FALSE

-- A company to which a liability is owed. who: 0 none of the listed persons run it; 1 the claimant is a director; 2 the other member is a director; 3 a qualifying young person is a director;
-- 4 a close relative (a parent) who lives with the claimant is a director; 5 the same relative does not live with the claimant; 6 the claimant is an owner with 10% of the shares;
-- 7 the claimant has 9% of the shares; 8 a close relative who lives with the claimant is an owner with 10% of the shares; 9 a person who is not a close relative is a director.
GIVEN who IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Company to which a liability is owed`
`uc3 test — a company` who MEANS
    `Company to which a liability is owed` WITH
        `the claimant as a possible owner or director` IS IF who EQUALS 1 THEN `uc3 test — a person who may run the company` TRUE EMPTY ELSE IF who EQUALS 6 THEN `uc3 test — a person who may run the company` FALSE (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 10 0) ELSE IF who EQUALS 7 THEN `uc3 test — a person who may run the company` FALSE (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 9 0) ELSE `uc3 test — a person who has nothing to do with the company`
        `the other member of the couple as a possible owner or director` IS IF who EQUALS 2 THEN `uc3 test — a person who may run the company` TRUE EMPTY ELSE `uc3 test — a person who has nothing to do with the company`
        `a qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible, as a possible owner or director` IS IF who EQUALS 3 THEN `uc3 test — a person who may run the company` TRUE EMPTY ELSE `uc3 test — a person who has nothing to do with the company`
        `a close relative of any of the above, as a possible owner or director` IS IF (who EQUALS 4) OR (who EQUALS 5) OR (who EQUALS 9) THEN `uc3 test — a person who may run the company` TRUE EMPTY ELSE IF who EQUALS 8 THEN `uc3 test — a person who may run the company` FALSE (LIST `uc3 test — a holder` TRUE 0 1 10 0) ELSE `uc3 test — a person who has nothing to do with the company`
        `the close relative as a possible close relative` IS `uc3 test — a relative` (IF who EQUALS 9 THEN `not a listed relation` ELSE `a parent`)
        `the close relative lives in the accommodation with the claimant` IS NOT (who EQUALS 5)

-- Expected for 6(1): the claimant, the other member and a qualifying young person who is a director each give TRUE; a close relative who lives with the claimant and is a director gives TRUE;
-- the same relative not living with the claimant gives FALSE; the claimant with 10% of the shares gives TRUE and with 9% gives FALSE; a close relative who lives with the claimant and holds 10% gives TRUE;
-- a director who is not a close relative gives FALSE; nobody gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the owners or directors of the company include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a company` 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the owners or directors of the company include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a company` 2) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the owners or directors of the company include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a company` 3) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the owners or directors of the company include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a company` 4) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the owners or directors of the company include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a company` 5) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the owners or directors of the company include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a company` 6) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the owners or directors of the company include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a company` 7) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the owners or directors of the company include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a company` 8) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the owners or directors of the company include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a company` 9) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6(1) — the owners or directors of the company include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a company` 0) EQUALS FALSE

-- Part 2 paragraph 7: liability to a trustee of a trust whose trustees or beneficiaries include the claimant, the other member, a child or qualifying young person for whom either is responsible,
-- or a close relative of any of them who lives in the accommodation with the claimant.
GIVEN trustee IS A BOOLEAN
      which IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Trust to which a liability is owed`
`uc3 test — a trust` trustee which MEANS
    `Trust to which a liability is owed` WITH
        `the liability is owed to a trustee of a trust` IS trustee
        `the trustees or beneficiaries include the claimant` IS which EQUALS 1
        `the trustees or beneficiaries include the other member of the couple` IS which EQUALS 2
        `the trustees or beneficiaries include a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible` IS which EQUALS 3
        `the trustees or beneficiaries include a close relative of any of the above who lives in the accommodation with the claimant` IS which EQUALS 4
-- Expected: each of the four gives TRUE; a trust none of them belongs to gives FALSE; a liability not owed to a trustee gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 7(1) — the trustees or beneficiaries include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a trust` TRUE 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 7(1) — the trustees or beneficiaries include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a trust` TRUE 2) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 7(1) — the trustees or beneficiaries include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a trust` TRUE 3) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 7(1) — the trustees or beneficiaries include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a trust` TRUE 4) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 7(1) — the trustees or beneficiaries include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a trust` TRUE 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 7(1) — the trustees or beneficiaries include a listed person` (`uc3 test — a trust` FALSE 1) EQUALS FALSE

-- The facts of a liability as Part 2 reads them. kind: the kind of payment; five: the creditor is a person within paragraph 5 (TRUE) or not (FALSE); six: the creditor is a company run by the claimant;
-- seven: a trust of which the claimant is a beneficiary; eight: a person in the claimant's household; flags: the claimant is treated under 5(1), 6(1), 7(1), 8(1) respectively as not liable to make the
-- rent (or owner-occupier) payments to the same creditor; none: there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of payment under Schedule 2`
      five IS A BOOLEAN
      six IS A BOOLEAN
      seven IS A BOOLEAN
      eight IS A BOOLEAN
      flag IS A BOOLEAN
      none IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a liability, as Part 2 reads them`
`uc3 test — facts about a liability` kind five six seven eight flag none MEANS
    `Facts about a liability, as Part 2 reads them` WITH
        `kind of payment` IS kind
        `the creditor as a possible person within paragraph 5` IS `uc3 test — a creditor` five (IF five THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        `the creditor as a possible company` IS `uc3 test — a company` (IF six THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        `the creditor as a possible trust` IS `uc3 test — a trust` seven (IF seven THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        `the creditor as a possible household member` IS `Household creditor` WITH `the liability is owed to a person who lives in the claimant's household` IS eight
        `the claimant is treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person` IS flag
        `the claimant is treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company` IS flag
        `the claimant is treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust` IS flag
        `the claimant is treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person` IS flag
        `there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments` IS none

-- Paragraph 5 (and the same shape in 6 and 7): rent payments owed to such a person give TRUE; service charge payments owed to the same person give TRUE only if the claimant is treated as not liable
-- to make the rent payments to that person (5(2)); owner-occupier payments give FALSE; a creditor outside the paragraph gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5 — the claimant is treated as not liable (close relative)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5 — the claimant is treated as not liable (close relative)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `service charge payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5 — the claimant is treated as not liable (close relative)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `service charge payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5 — the claimant is treated as not liable (close relative)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `owner-occupier payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 5 — the claimant is treated as not liable (close relative)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6 — the claimant is treated as not liable (company)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6 — the claimant is treated as not liable (company)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `service charge payments` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 6 — the claimant is treated as not liable (company)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `service charge payments` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 7 — the claimant is treated as not liable (trust)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 7 — the claimant is treated as not liable (trust)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `service charge payments` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 7 — the claimant is treated as not liable (trust)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `service charge payments` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Paragraph 8: owner-occupier payments owed to a person in the claimant's household give TRUE; service charge payments give TRUE if the claimant is treated as not liable to make the owner-occupier
-- payments to that person (8(2)), or there is no liability for rent payments or owner-occupier payments at all (8(3)); otherwise FALSE; rent payments owed to a household member give FALSE (paragraph 8 does not name them).
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable (household)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `owner-occupier payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable (household)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `service charge payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable (household)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `service charge payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable (household)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `service charge payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable (household)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable (household)` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `owner-occupier payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Paragraphs 5 to 8 together: any one of them. Expected: a rent payment to a close relative gives TRUE; a rent payment to a stranger gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 paras 5 to 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable to make the payments` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 paras 5 to 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable to make the payments` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- Paragraph 9: the claimant is treated as not liable for any amount that is an increase in the sum otherwise payable, resulting from arrears; but not if paragraphs 5 to 8 already apply (9(2)).
-- Expected: 40 pounds of arrears increase gives 40 when none of 5 to 8 applies; 0 when one does.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 9 — the amount for which the claimant is treated as not liable because of arrears` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) 40 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 9 — the amount for which the claimant is treated as not liable because of arrears` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) 40 EQUALS 0
-- Paragraph 10: the liability was contrived (the Secretary of State is satisfied), unless paragraphs 5 to 8 already apply (10(2)).
-- Expected: contrived and none of 5 to 8 gives TRUE; contrived and one of 5 to 8 applies gives FALSE; not contrived gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 10 — the claimant is treated as not liable because the liability was contrived` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 10 — the claimant is treated as not liable because the liability was contrived` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 10 — the claimant is treated as not liable because the liability was contrived` (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The whole: liable in fact, or treated as liable under Part 1, and not treated as not liable under Part 2 (fork U3-F15: Part 2 prevails).
-- part1: liable in fact; the person liable (a child); failure: all four conditions (when failed); rent free: not asked here.
GIVEN inFact IS A BOOLEAN
      child IS A BOOLEAN
      failure IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Part 1 facts about a liability`
`uc3 test — Part 1 facts` inFact child failure MEANS
    `Part 1 facts about a liability` WITH
        `the claimant is liable in fact` IS inFact
        `the person who is liable` IS `Person who is liable to make the payments` WITH
            `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible` IS child
            `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member` IS FALSE
        `claim basis` IS `a single claimant`
        `claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4)` IS FALSE
        `failure to pay` IS `Failure to pay by the person who is liable` WITH
            `the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so` IS failure
            `the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation` IS failure
            `the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements` IS failure
            `it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments` IS failure
        waiver IS `Waiver of liability for repair work` WITH
            `the liability to make payments is waived by the person to whom the liability is owed` IS FALSE
            `the waiver is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation` IS FALSE
            `the works are works which the person to whom the liability is owed would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out` IS FALSE
        `the arrangements provide for rent free periods` IS FALSE
        `the period` IS `Period of the arrangements` WITH `the renter has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6` IS FALSE

-- Expected: liable in fact and nothing in Part 2 gives TRUE; not liable in fact but a child is liable (Part 1 paragraph 1) gives TRUE; not liable in fact but the person liable has failed to pay (paragraph 2) gives TRUE;
-- not liable in fact and nothing in Part 1 gives FALSE; liable in fact but the creditor is a close relative (paragraph 5) gives FALSE; Part 1 applying does not rescue a Part 2 case (U3-F15) gives FALSE;
-- liable in fact but contrived gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 — the claimant is liable to make the payments` (`uc3 test — Part 1 facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE) (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 — the claimant is liable to make the payments` (`uc3 test — Part 1 facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE) (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 — the claimant is liable to make the payments` (`uc3 test — Part 1 facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE) (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 — the claimant is liable to make the payments` (`uc3 test — Part 1 facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 — the claimant is liable to make the payments` (`uc3 test — Part 1 facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE) (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 — the claimant is liable to make the payments` (`uc3 test — Part 1 facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE) (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 — the claimant is liable to make the payments` (`uc3 test — Part 1 facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE) (`uc3 test — facts about a liability` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
